course: dictionary
lesson: 9884
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. Taffy is one of these words. In the USA and Canada, taffy is a soft, chewy sweet, and «salt-water taffy» is a famous kind sold at the seaside.
explain: Taffy can also be a name. In two of Kipling's Just So Stories, Taffy is a clever, cheeky Stone-Age girl. She draws a picture-letter for her mother and helps her father Tegumai invent the alphabet. Look for a capital letter and clues about people in the sentence to know that it is a name.
explain: Some meanings are old or rude. In old UK speech, taffy was a nickname for a Welsh person, and many Welsh people find it insulting. When you meet a word with a meaning that feels wrong, check a dictionary and never use a word that could hurt someone.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word.
fact: «Taffy» means a soft, chewy sweet made by boiling sugar and pulling it until it is shiny and stretchy.
fact: In some places in the UK, old use: taffy means toffee.
fact: «Taffy» is also a girl's name in two of Kipling's Just So Stories.
fact: «Taffy» as an old nickname for a Welsh person is rude and insulting, so never use it.
exercise: A child at the seaside says, «I want a bag of salt-water taffy.» What is taffy here? | A small wooden boat | A kind of seagull | A sandy hat | *A soft, chewy sweet
exercise: «Tegumai shows Taffy the big secret.» Who is Taffy in this story? | A Welsh singer | A Roman soldier in Surrey | A talking carp | *A clever, cheeky Stone-Age girl
exercise: «There they find Taffy making daisy-chains.» Taffy is a name here. How can you tell? | It means a party | It is a sweet you can eat | *It starts with a capital letter and names a girl | It is a kind of spear
test: A «taffy pull» is what? | *A party where people pull warm taffy | A kind of tug-of-war with ropes | A race to the sea | A Stone-Age dance
test: Which meaning of taffy is rude and should never be used? | Toffee in some places | A soft, chewy sweet | A girl in a Kipling story | *An old nickname for a Welsh person
exam: The Head Chief says Taffy has made a great invention which men will one day call writing. What is Taffy's invention most likely to be? | A taffy pull party | A Roman road | *A picture-letter that began writing | A seaside sweet shop
